        "id": 49895,
        "name": "Déjà Vu I & II: The Casebooks of Ace Harding",
        "summary": "Take on two thrilling mysteries in one Game Pak!\n\nLife is never boring when you assume the role of Ace Harding, private detective. In Deja Vu I, you will scramble down the dark alleys of Chicago, searching for a cure for you amnesia and a killer who has framed you for a brutal murder. After solving the first case, you'll uncover a few loose strings that gradually unrabel into Deja Vu II. Trapped in the slimy town of Last Vegas, you find yourself dealing with a notorious mob leader who makes you an offer you can't refuse.\n\n-Two detailed graphic adventure games in one Game Boy Color Game Pak!\n-Detailed commands for interacting with anyone or anything!\n-Return to the scene of the crime, or any of the other 140 locations!\n-Sort out the real evidence from the red herrings and over 80 other items!\n-Battery-backed save option for up to three save game files!",
        "cover_url": "https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/xitd4dprofblbaiwqxiw.jpg",
        "release_date": 946684800,
        "rating": null,
        "rating_count": null,
        "genres": "Adventure",
        "platform_ids": "22",
        "external_url": "https://www.igdb.com/games/deja-vu-i-and-ii-the-casebooks-of-ace-harding",
        "cached_at": 1772527929
      },
      {
        "id": 49896,
        "name": "Deer Hunter",
        "summary": "The popular pursuit of hunting comes to the portable screen in DEER HUNTER for the Game Boy Color. You play as a hunter looking to catch a nice trophy in one of four different areas using three different weapons. Hunt deer with a shotgun, a rifle, or a bow, using slightly different tactics with each. If you want to be successful, you'll have to use real-world hunting strategies. Search for droppings or other signs of movement to find the best area to wait in. Once there, use one of an assortment of tools to help you catch your prey: mask your odor with a cover scent, use a tree stand to camouflage yourself, or lure the deer with a powerful musk, a deer call, or an antler rattle. It's up to you to decide how to catch the deer; some methods are more efficient than others, so you'll have to find the one that works best for you. Detailed graphics and digitized sound round out the experience for would-be hunters.",
        "cover_url": "https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/jgj2vcn6tispqzglqjot.jpg",
        "release_date": 948499200,
        "rating": null,
        "rating_count": null,
        "genres": "Simulator|Sport",
        "platform_ids": "22,8",
        "external_url": "https://www.igdb.com/games/deer-hunter",
        "cached_at": 1772527929
      },
      {
        "id": 49897,
        "name": "Cubix: Robots For Everyone - Race 'N Robots",
        "summary": "Robots in everyday life? Believe it, folks. That's the reality of the cool cartoon series, CUBIX: Robots for Everyone. The story follows the adventures of Connor a human boy and his robot, Cubix, through Bubble Town. Attempting to repair damaged robots and ward off evil beings, the pair encounters a whole cast of wacky characters every week. The game puts its emphasis on the racing aspects of the series, sending you to Bubble Town's racing championship series. Your arch-nemesis, Dr. K, has a converted racer named Kolossal in the competition, and your goal is to earn the right to defeat it. Choose to race as any of your favorite series characters, including Hop2ix, Brutix, Don-Don, Diagnostix, and Cubix. You'll be able to customize your racers to fit your liking, using elements like Grav-grip, Zero G, and other series-based power-ups to defy gravity and reach top speeds. Full of cool options game modes, and colorful graphics, Race N Robots is not to be missed.",
        "cover_url": "https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/oq8b5eyintxemqcd4cdj.jpg",
        "release_date": 1005177600,
        "rating": null,
        "rating_count": null,
        "genres": "Racing",
        "platform_ids": "22,6,7",
        "external_url": "https://www.igdb.com/games/cubix-robots-for-everyone-race-n-robots",
        "cached_at": 1772527929
      },
      {
        "id": 49898,
        "name": "Chase H.Q.: Secret Police",
        "summary": "The chase is on in CHASE HQ: Secret Police for the Game Boy Color. Loosely adapted from the arcade game of the same name, CHASE HQ is a unique mix of racing and action for one or two players. In the One-Player mode, you'll lead a handpicked team of undercover cops, each with unique talents. You'll be shown what kind of vehicle the suspect is driving, and then you'll hit the streets to find him. When you finally locate the perp, you'll switch to a behind-the-vehicle view as you try to shoot or bump the criminal off the road. Once you've managed to lower their life-bar far enough, they'll pull over and you'll make the arrest. There are 10 levels of single-player action, so you'll be plenty busy as you try to collar the criminals. You can also grab a friend to play Head-to-Head using a link cable, with one person playing the cop and the other playing the bad guy.",
        "cover_url": "https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/co5v6f.jpg",
        "release_date": 962323200,
        "rating": null,
